<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5772" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιδέξιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ambidextrous</i> (cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφαρίστερος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				7.43
			</span></i> (wrongly expl. by Glaucias ap.<i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				7.50
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1134b34
			</span></i>; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιδέξιος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hippon.
				83
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως, παίζειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Polem.Hist.
					45
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>ready to take with either hand,</i> i.e. <i>taking either of
				two things, indifferent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Trag.Adesp.
				355
			</span></i> ( =
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				360
			</span></i>); so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιδεξίως ἔχει</span> it
			is <i>indifferent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				266
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>two-edged,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίδηρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					780
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> metaph.,
				<i>double-meaning, ambiguous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρηστήριον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.92
				</span></i>
			.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έ</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>JTr.</u>
				43
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>on either hand, with both hands,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀκμαῖς</span> with <i>both</i>
			hands <i>at once,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				1243
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρείσατ᾽ . . πλευρὸν ἀμφιδέξιον
					ἐμφύντε τῷ φύσαντι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OC</u>
					1112
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφιδέξια, τά,</span>
			<i>bracelets,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>: sg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφίδεξιν</span> (sic) <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.238a
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
